cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MetriPlane, please cite the software release."
title: "MetriPlane: Open Research Software for Camera-First Planar Metric State Streaming, Replay, Zone Analytics, and Physical-Space Auditing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Parkkinen"
    given-names: "Miko"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-06-13"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Miko997/metriplane"
url: "https://github.com/Miko997/metriplane"
abstract: >-
  MetriPlane is open research software for camera-first planar metric state
  streaming, deterministic replay, zone analytics, and observe-only physical
  operations auditing. The software detects fiducial markers, maps observations
  into metric XY coordinates, supports multi-camera fusion and tracking,
  evaluates spatial contracts, emits incidents, builds replayable evidence
  bundles, and exposes a read-only Command Center for operator review. The
  v0.2.0 release adds Sentinel, physical regression testing, camera trust
  analysis, local operator answers, and integration adapters while preserving
  the historical v0.1.3 benchmark evidence baseline.
keywords:
  - research software
  - digital twins
  - robotics
  - industrial automation
  - physical observability
  - deterministic replay
  - zone analytics
  - ArUco
  - planar homography
  - reproducibility
